  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "`assets/skills/habeas/SKILL.md` is a bundled skill with front matter, so it is a site of `requirements.cli.skill_conventions`. Its `description` says when to use it in terms of the user's task: \"Use at the start of any work in a project that tracks requirements with Habeas\", followed by concrete signals of such a project. It then names other bundled skills (habeas-requirements, habeas-refactor, habeas-evidence, habeas-bootstrap-requirements) to route to by task type, which the requirement allows with MAY. It also says it is the reference for syntax and the `habeas status` and `habeas info` commands. The requirement defines no violation queries here. I found no gap.",
